    "reply": "I added `tests/test_payments.py` with 10 tests. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` passes, with 8 normal passes and 2 expected failures. I didn't change anything under `shop/`.\n\n- **`line_total`:** price times quantity, and a zero quantity.\n- **`order_total`:** an empty order, tax on a single line, several lines summed before tax, and rounding to two decimals.\n- **`refund`:** a partial refund and a full refund.\n\n`refund()` has no input validation, so I wrote two tests for it and marked them `@unittest.expectedFailure`:\n- A refund larger than the order total returns a negative balance, for example `refund(100, 120)` gives `-20`.\n- A negative refund amount increases the balance, for example `refund(100, -10)` gives `110`.\n\nI assumed `refund()` should raise `ValueError` in both cases. Say if you want a different behavior. The tests will start failing once the bug is fixed, which is the cue to remove the decorators.",
